WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
French has a word for 'him':

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:02.790
«Je le vois».

3
00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.030
I see him.

4
00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:07.100
English uses 'him' after 'with' as well.

5
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.600
I'm going out with him.

6
00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:13.240
So for 'with him', just put that
same little word after «avec».

7
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.270
Easy. Except French never does.

8
00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:20.450
And the usual French 'me'
can't follow «avec» either.

9
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.350
So what does French put
after «avec» instead,

10
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.330
and why? In this mission,

11
00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:30.650
you'll line up eight pronouns in two
columns and hunt for the differences.

12
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:32.610
Then you'll see what happens to 'him',

13
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.690
'her' and 'them' after a word like 'with'.

14
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.920
Your mission: find the
word French uses instead.
